Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 python3 (>= 3.12),
# python3-bcrypt hashes the replacement for the seeded administrator password
# (bootstrap-admin) and the break-glass administrator import-o19 creates.
 python3-bcrypt,
# mariadb-client (not -core): every database verb drives the mariadb CLI
# (db, db-dump, db-users, db-migrate's collation probe, the o19 importer).
 mariadb-client (>= 1:11.4),
# ss, for the listening-socket assertions in `carlos-ctl check`.
 iproute2,
# ps, for the "no component runs as root" assertion in `carlos-ctl check`.
 procps,
# curl: the live front-door, WAF and DrugRef probes in `carlos-ctl check`.
 curl
Recommends:
# jq makes `carlos-ctl waf tail` readable; it degrades to raw JSON without it.
 jq
# Deliberately NO Depends on carlos-emr: carlos-emr depends on this package,
# and a dependency back would be a cycle. The CLI checks for the application
# package at run time and says so when it is absent.
#
# Through 2026.08.0~alpha15 the CLI shipped INSIDE carlos-emr (the same
# /usr/sbin/carlos-ctl, the carlosctl compatibility symlink and both man
# pages). Every earlier carlos-emr has to hand those files over (Replaces)
# and must not stay configured beside this package (Breaks): Policy 7.6.1.
# A FIXED version: the first carlos-emr RELEASE that no longer ships them
# is 2026.08.0~alpha16 (built from release/2026.08), and `~alpha16~` sorts
# just below it, so alpha16, an rc or the final all sit above the boundary.
# Developer snapshots are versioned 2026.09.0~snapshotN and sort ABOVE every
# 2026.08 version, so a PRE-split snapshot (snapshot24 and earlier, from the
# develop/main tree) is not covered: dpkg would refuse to overwrite its
# /usr/sbin/carlos-ctl. That move is a downgrade in dpkg terms and is not a
# supported upgrade source anyway (see carlos-emr's debian/control); on such
# a host `apt remove carlos-emr` first, then install the split pair. A range
# cannot say "below alpha16 OR below snapshot25" -- each Breaks entry is
# independent, so a second entry would break the split snapshots too.
Breaks:
 carlos-emr (<< 2026.08.0~alpha16~)
Replaces:
 carlos-emr (<< 2026.08.0~alpha16~)
Description: administration command for the CARLOS EMR Debian deployment
 carlos-ctl administers a CARLOS EMR host installed from the carlos-emr
 package: the deployment check, service lifecycle, schema migration and
 database accounts, certificates, the ModSecurity front door, backups and
 restore drills, and the experimental OSCAR 19 clinic import.
 .
 The carlos-emr maintainer scripts call the same verbs an administrator does,
 so provisioning logic exists in exactly one place. carlos-emr depends on
 this package; the two version independently, and the CLI applies whatever
 schema the installed carlos-emr ships.
 .
 The command is carlos-ctl(8); the older spelling carlosctl still works.
